  "name": "A New Century · political transitions",
  "start": "2000-01-01",
  "description": "Govern for five years: keep household needs met, services funded and government stable. Country play continues after political transitions. Relative food/energy prices are authored rules-3 model assumptions, not sourced historical prices. The original fixed-price pack is retained for classic saves. Borrowing authority, consent delays and emergency political costs are authored rules-4 assumptions, not a reproduction of historical debt law. Earlier market and classic packs remain available for their original campaigns. Constitutional transitions use authored rules-5 templates, backing thresholds, costs and inertia rather than sourced historical amendment law. Starter AI prefers its opening governing form; fictional fixtures demonstrate alternative preferences. Earlier campaigns retain their original packs.",
